{
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.AngryDemonfistPlayerLoss.BarelyStanding": "You stumble back, barely capable of standing up. Your vision blurs as you struggle to keep focus on your opponent. Demonfist shakes his head, scorn noticeable in his eyes.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.AngryDemonfistPlayerLoss.CrowdRoars": "[pg]The crowd roars in enthusiasm, the sound deafening your ears and intensifying your confusion. The next few moments appear to happen in slow motion: Demonfist charging at you with a readied fist, you breathing deeply and attempting to lift your arms to defend yourself, his fist hitting your jaw like a cannon ball."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.AngryDemonfistPlayerLoss.FuckedOrStupid": "[say: [Ringname], I gotta tell you. You're either fucked in the head, or you think that fighting dirty will eventually pay off. It won't. This is just going to keep happening, and happening. And every single time...]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.AngryDemonfistPlayerLoss.PunchesTurned": "[say: What's going on, \"[Ringname]\"? Did one of my punches turn your brain to mush? You knew the rules, damn it!]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.AngryDemonfistPlayerLoss.ShrugsCrowd": "[pg]He looks towards the crowd and playfully shrugs, as if to show that you forced his hand. The audience reaction is split between cheers and laughs, and Demonfist himself can't help but crack a smile as well. [say: Very well then, you all know what cheaters deserve!] He says, tensing his right fist."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.AngryDemonfistPlayerLoss.WhatWasPoint": "[say: What was the point of all this? Are you too stupid to follow simple rules or did you get scared after the fight started? Scum.] He looks towards the crowd and smiles. [say: [he]'ll get what [he] deserves, won't [he]?]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.AngryDemonfistPlayerLoss.WorldShifting": "[pg]You barely feel the world shifting around you as you hit the floor of the ring. Soon after, the world blackens."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.AngryDemonfistPlayerLoss2.BodilyFluids": "The smell of bodily fluids and rotten food assaults your nostrils, consciousness rudely invading your mind once again. One by one, your limbs and muscles make themselves known to you again, mostly through soreness and pain."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.AngryDemonfistPlayerLoss2.MaybeLater": "[pg]Maybe later, you think to yourself."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.AngryDemonfistPlayerLoss2.ThrownInCell": "[pg]You open your eyes and notice you've been thrown in a gutter, most likely the place where the denizens of the Bazaar dump their trash. You groan as you get up and check your equipment, all of which is surprisingly where it's supposed to be. You brush some unmentionable fluids off from your person and look forwards to the edge of the Bazaar."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.BackToBazaar.ShakesHead": "You narrow your eyes and shake your head before turning away from the tent. You don't really fancy gratuitous violence now, especially when you might be on the receiving end of it."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.ChallengeBegins.NodsAccepts": "[pg]You nod and accept. He smiles. [say: Very nice. Well, hit me with all you've got! The fight starts when you attack me. Come on! Give me a challenge, and give the crowd a show!]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.ChallengeBegins.StretchesArm": "[pg]Demonfist stretches an arm towards you and motions for you to attack him. The crowd cheers for the two of you and you prepare to strike. <b>It's a fight!</b>"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.ChallengeBegins.TakesGemPouch": "[pg]You take a gem pouch from your gear as the crowd parts in front of you, giving you a clear path towards the ring. You tense your muscles and climb the ring, quickly tossing the pouch to Demonfist when you enter it. As usual, he immediately tosses it towards the rhino-morph. You stare down at the champion, and he does the same to you. [say: If you don't know the rules, it's simple,] he says, cracking his knuckles. [say: You can use whatever weapons and dirty tricks you want against me. Go nuts. The one rule I have is no magic. I see you casting a spell and it won't be a fun sparring match anymore. I'm pretty sure the crowd here won't take it too well either. So, get it?]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.ChallengeBegins.YellsRingName": "You raise a hand and yell out your ring name with confidence. The crowd turns to face you while Demonfist looks at you with interest, fingers running through his chin as he smiles. [say: Very well then, [ringname]. Show me the goods and climb into the ring. Let's see what you got to offer!]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.ChatOrigins.AgreesPointsOut": "[pg]You agree, but point out it's still a good point to start a conversation with. He scratches his chin, pondering for a moment before nodding. [say: Yeah, alright, though it's nothing special. Where do I start?][pg]He covers his mouth and burps, showing surprising etiquette for someone as rough looking as him, before tapping his fingers on the table and starting his story. [say: Most of my life is forgettable and plain, so you're probably looking for the more interesting, \"demonic\" business. As much as running a gang of marauders can be considered exclusively demonic, anyway.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.ChatOrigins.AnotherGulp": "[pg]He takes another gulp, stopping abruptly as he notices his mug is empty. He lays it on the table and tilts his gaze towards you as he lifts his arm and asks for another."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.ChatOrigins.AsksOrigins": "You ask the demon about his origins. What leads a demon like him to open a fighting pit in the Bazaar?"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.ChatOrigins.BoredOfRunning": "[pg]You nod and ask him what made him get bored of running his gang. He takes a large gulp of his mug, wipes his mouth and sighs."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.ChatOrigins.GroansLightly": "[pg]He groans lightly. [say:Shit, not sure what to say. We roamed around, pillaged, killed, raped. Eventually I got bored of it and settled here.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.ChatOrigins.HeChuckles": "[pg]He chuckles. [say: Hah, Lethice, good one. Don't believe I've seen more than a glimpse of Lethice's cleavage from two hundred feet away, and I don't believe she ever gave a shit about what I did. No, that's not how it worked for me. Back in those days it was a free for all, pretty much. You took what you could get. I could get more than most, and other demons just naturally followed.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.ChatOrigins.HeScoffs": "[pg]He scoffs, leaning back into his chair a bit. [say: Bit of a boring question, isn't it?]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.ChatOrigins.HeSmiles": "[pg]He smiles. [say: Suppose I was, yeah. So one day I disbanded my gang and used whatever loot I had left to build that joint you call a fighting pit. Nice retirement home for a \"veteran\" bored of punching weaklings.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.ChatOrigins.InItForFight": "[pg]You point out that it seems he was in it for the fights, rather than the sex or the riches. "
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.ChatOrigins.KeepGoing": "[pg]You tell him to keep going, asking for details on his gang."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.ChatOrigins.LaughsRemembering": "[pg][say: The beginning was great, don't get me wrong. Every village we raided had its share of capable fighters willing to fight tooth and nail to protect themselves. Had several brushes with death in those days.] He laughs, probably from remembering one of these encounters. [say: After a while, though, it became pretty clear we won, and nobody was around to really challenge us--me--anymore. The occasional demon trying to take my place got my blood pumping a bit, but even that faded away when my kill count got too high.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.ChatOrigins.NotSureTelling": "[pg]You're not sure if telling him your true origins is the best idea."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.ChatOrigins.ProdsMore": "[pg]That's it? You prod him for information, asking him how he got to rule a band of demons in the first place. Was it Lethice that granted him his group?"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.ChatOrigins.YourStory": "[pg][say: What about you, [name]? What's your story?] He asks, not particularly curious about your answer either way."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.ChatOriginsAnswer.DeepBreath": "You take a deep breath and look him in the eyes, causing a brow to arch on his face. After a moment to think, you start laying out your entire story. You describe Ingnam, the Elders, their process to choose a sacrifice, the portal at Mount Ilgast, your preparation to walk through it, Zetaz, the camp, everything, down to the most minute of details."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.ChatOriginsAnswer.GoneWorse": "[pg]Could have gone worse."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.ChatOriginsAnswer.HeShrugs": "[pg]He shrugs. [say: Suit yourself, then. I was hoping this conversation wouldn't be so one sided, But I can't ask you to lie just to be more interesting.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.ChatOriginsAnswer.HuhAmazing": "[pg][say: Huh, amazing. Never knew Lethice secretly followed your orders, or that the Old Seers, whoever they are, foretold of your arrival from the stars 5000 years ago. Also, I'm pretty sure people all over Mareth would have noticed if someone punched a volcano so hard it erupted, but maybe I just wasn't paying attention that day.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.ChatOriginsAnswer.NoneOfBusiness": "You tell him your story is none of his business. He laughs heartily. [say: Wow, right after asking me for mine, too. You're an asshole, I'll save a punch for that one next time we fight.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.ChatOriginsAnswer.NotAboutToTell": "You're not about to tell him your real story. You think for a moment and tell him the most grandiose, insane story you could think of, remembering every tale ever told to you in Ingnam and adding some Marethian elements to it. Demonfist is surprisingly captured by it, though from the look on his face he's more interested in your creativity than anything else."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.ChatOriginsAnswer.NotMuchInteresting": "You tell him there's really not much interesting about your past at all. Hardly something worthwhile to share over a mug of ale."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.ChatOriginsAnswer.QuarterDrunk": "[pg]When you're done, you notice he's a quarter of the way through another mug of ale, looking at a random direction while enjoying his drink. He snaps back to attention when he notices you're finished. [say: Damn, that's very interesting. Everything about it is very cool. Yeah.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.ChatOriginsAnswer.WaitressArrives": "[pg]The waitress arrives at your table and gives him another mug before taking the empty one and leaving. He sips on it briefly before facing you again. [say: Got anything else to ask? I'm hoping this conversation will be less one sided.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.ChatOriginsAnswer.WaitressArrivesAgain": "[pg]The waitress arrives at your table and gives him another mug before taking the empty one and leaving. He sips on it briefly before facing you again. [say: Got anything else to ask? I'm hoping this conversation will be less one sided.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.ChatOriginsAnswer.WaitressArrivesThird": "[pg]The waitress arrives at your table and gives him another mug before taking the empty one and leaving. He sips on it briefly before facing you again. [say: You're an interesting fellow, [name]. Yeah, \"interesting\" is a good word.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.DefendTitle.AssuresHim": "[pg]You assure him that it wasn't. He nods and extends his hand for you to shake."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.DefendTitle.DogNameIntro": "[pg][say: [Ringname], this is <DOG_NAME>. And I believe the current champion doesn't need introduction, right?]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.DefendTitle.FlashesGrin": "[pg][say: Correct,] the dog-morph says, flashing a rivalrous smile. [say: Got quite surprised when the news of Demonfist getting decked reached me. He took a few of my teeth out a few months ago, so I had to see what this new champion was all about. Hope it wasn't a lucky break.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.DefendTitle.KnowEachOther": "[pg][say: Well, you already know each other, no reason to waste time. Onwards to the fighting, it's what the crowd wants, and it's what makes us money."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.DefendTitle.PursesLips": "[pg]He purses his leathery lips and whistles to the crowd, causing a pair of black ears to poke out from the sea of people, turning towards the rhino. <DOG_NAME> surges from the crowd after a while, looking confident, but not overly so. Ozzie places a hand on both your shoulders before energetically shaking them, accompanied by a deep chuckle. It slightly annoys you, and you can tell it annoys the grizzled dog-morph as well."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.DefendTitle.WantsToFight": "You tell Ozzie that you want to fight. A greedy smile appears in his face. [say: Brilliant. Having the champion fight should improve attendance today quite a bit.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.DemonFistTentDescription.ConstantFlow": "[pg]The constant flow of demons towards an out of sight tent reminds you of Demonfist's arena. Its popularity never decreases, apparently."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.DemonFistTentDescription.DemonsBeeline": "[pg]Several demons appear to be making a bee line towards a location you can't quite see from where you're standing. From the sheer amount of them, it seems to be worth a visit."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.EnterTheLine.CanDoIt": "[pg][say: I-I can do it! I get mocked a lot by all the other demons here, but once the news that Miffix the Imp beat Demonfist spreads, they will all respect me! The succubi will be all over me, the other imps will be afraid of me, and I bet Lethice will even hire me to be a captain in her army, making me the most respected imp since Zetaz!]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.EnterTheLine.EntersLine": "Curious, you decide to enter the rather long line. You tap a fidgety imp in front of you on the shoulder, causing him to turn to face you with suspicion, and ask him what the line is for. He groans in a high pitched voice, but answers all the same."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.EnterTheLine.GoesSilent": "[pg][say: I'm going to try my luck, I am. I've collected enough gems]--he goes silent for a moment, mouthing out \"five hundred\" with incredulous eyes--[say: to pay for one round with him, and I've watched enough fights to know all his moves. I can do it!]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.EnterTheLine.MentionsVacancy": "[pg]You nod, and tell him there might even be a vacancy in Lethice's army, considering you killed Zetaz yourself. The imp laughs nervously. [say: H-heh, of course you did. You even match the Champion's descr--] His eyes widen, and he remains silent for a moment before quickly turning to face the line."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.EnterTheLine.StupidOrNot": "[pg][say: You stupid or something? This is Demonfist's arena! You either watch him fight for free, or make a bet to be part of the entertainment.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.EnterTheLine.WhichOfTwo": "[pg]You nod and ask him which of the two he plans to do. He looks around, somewhat nervous, and whispers into your ear."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.EnterTheLine.WhyRiskMoney": "[pg]You ask him why he would risk that much money on a fight, considering he's not exactly all that physically intimidating himself and that some of the bruised demons leaving the tent are quite muscular. He is visibly offended, his pointy ears drooping down as he chews on his lip."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.EnterTheLine.WishesLuck": "[pg]You nod and wish him good luck in his insane gamble. He turns to face the line again."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.EnterTheLine2.AudienceSilent": "[pg]For a few seconds, the audience remains silent. The thought to jump into the ring yourself crosses your mind, but someone else screams their own name before you can do anything. \"Miffix\", the voice yells."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.EnterTheLine2.BetterFool": "[pg][say: Better fool than craven.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.EnterTheLine2.CrimsonFalls": "[pg]The crimson demon falls like a rock to the floor of the makeshift ring, and the audience's anxious silence breaks into celebration. You do your best to shuffle your way to a somewhat comfortable spot with a decent view, and end up losing sight of the diminutive Miffix in the process."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.EnterTheLine2.GoodOne": "[pg][say: Good one,] The indigo demon says, breathing heavily. [say: Fast, smart, but definitely a glass jaw. How many has it been today?]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.EnterTheLine2.LongWait": "The two of you suffer through the rather long wait, periodically hearing the sounds of amazed crowds, always followed by a battered and broken demon leaving the tent. Every minute that passes makes you wonder if the wait could possibly be worth it, but you push through, rationalizing that you've already wasted too much time to just go back now. After a few more minutes, you finally enter the tent."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.EnterTheLine2.MiffixEnters": "[pg]Miffix shuffles through the crowd and enters the ring, with some difficulty."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.EnterTheLine2.MiffixIsIt": "[pg][say: Miffix, is it? I can't see you! Come onto the ring and let's see what you have,] Demonfist yells out. A hole forms in the packed crowd, revealing the emaciated Miffix, who immediately prompts laughter from the audience, some of it subdued, some of it not. [say: Come on people, don't underestimate an opponent!] Demonfist says, waving at the imp to climb into the ring. [say: Wouldn't be the first time I fought someone that's much faster or stronger than they look. And if he's a fool, well, the way I see it...]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.EnterTheLine2.ScreamsSeven": "[pg]The audience screams \"seven\" in unison, prompting a smile from the demon. [say: Alright, alright. I think I've got one more in me for today.] He gets up, much to the crowd's amazement, stretching his shoulders and massaging his bandage-covered knuckles, the fabric deeply stained with blood from previous fighters. [say: Are any of you in the audience]--he points to the crowd with a confident smile--[say: brave enough to try your skills against Demonfist?] He rolls his eyes after saying his title, perhaps aware of how silly it sounds."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.EnterTheLine2.StuffyAir": "[pg]The air inside the tent is stuffy, pregnant with the smell of sweat and blood, and the heat is almost unbearable. At the center you see a makeshift boxing ring, evidently built in a hurry. You see a well built, indigo-colored demon inside, as well as a significantly skinnier demon with crimson-colored skin. The indigo demon is currently uppercutting the crimson demon's jaw, enough speed and strength within the move to make the entire audience cringe with empathetic pain."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.EnterTheLine2.WavesHand": "[pg]The indigo demon waves his hand, prompting a rhino-morph to jump into the ring and grab the other demon, who is still knocked out cold. He takes a waterskin from one of corners of the ring, drinking a bit of it and pouring the rest over his head. He pulls a stool from outside the ring, places it on the floor and sits on it, slumping in relaxation."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.FollowTheLine.FollowsLine": "You follow the conspicuous line of demons to its source, a rather unassuming tent that does little to distinguish itself from the other stores in the Bazaar. One thing you do notice as you approach, however, is that quite a few demons and other creatures are leaving the tent, most of them bruised and bleeding. Looking down, you notice several troubling patches of blood and sweat covering the ground. Whatever happens in that tent, it's violent."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.IntroDogFight.AddressesCrowd": "[pg][say: Ladies and gentlemen,] Ozzie says, addressing the crowd. [say: Demonfist has disappeared, but the spectacle hasn't! On one side, [ringname], the current champion, the one that finally toppled Demonfist!] Ozzie waits for the crowd's reaction before continuing and it comes quickly, with even more energetic shouting praising your name. [say: And on the other, a sudden challenger that has already proved himself by defeating many experienced fighters! <DOG_NAME>!] The dog-morph lazily lifts his hand to answer his name being called, and the crowd is amicable enough to him, praising his courage."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.IntroDogFight.LeadToRing": "Ozzie takes the two of you towards the ring. The crowd becomes elated and energetic as you step in, with quite a few of them shouting your name in unison. You can't help but feel energized and motivated, even if your frame doesn't stretch far beyond this makeshift ring in the Bazaar."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.IntroDogFight.NoMoreDelays": "[pg][say: Well, no more delays, then! A fight you want and a fight you'll get!] Ozzie says, looking at you and then at <DOG_NAME>, checking if the two of you are ready. Both of you nod, confirming it. The rhino-morph lifts his right arm. [say: Ready? FIGHT!] He shouts before swinging his arm down. It's a fight!"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.IntroDogFight.RefusesHand": "You refuse to shake his hand. He narrows his eyes, analyzing you and trying to understand why. Ozzie breaks the tension with a laugh. [say: Nice! The crowd loves these dramatic fights. Build up some anger and let it out on the ring!][pg]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.IntroDogFight.ShakesHand": "You shake his hand, eliciting a smile from him. [say: Hm, the crowd prefers some drama, but a plain fight works too,] Ozzie says. [say: Onwards towards the ring, then.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.JustWatchFight.CrowdErupts": "[pg]The crowd erupts into cheering as the champion raises his fist in celebration. Another victory for Demonfist, but the display has certainly fueled the courage of many would-be challengers."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.JustWatchFight.CrowdShock": "[pg]The crowd goes silent in shock as Demonfist's opponent unleashes a decisive attack. The following moment seems to play in slow motion, with Demonfist narrowly avoiding the crushing move and swiftly countering before the challenger can raise his defences, knocking {0} to the ground, where {1} remains."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.JustWatchFight.DecentShow": "[pg]Demonfist's new adversary puts on a decent show, but it's clear from the beginning what the result would be. A few superficial hits on the champion is all {0} manages before kissing the floor of the ring. Decent entertainment, all things considered."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.JustWatchFight.HadFairShare": "[pg]A few minutes later, you decide you've gotten your fair share of fighting for the moment, on the spectator's side, at least, and leave the tent."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.JustWatchFight.KeepSpectating": "You decide it would be best to just continue spectating for now.[pg]It takes mere moments for another person to throw their hat--and gems--into the ring."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.JustWatchFight.NewChallenger": "[pg]A new challenger steps into the ring, and it quickly becomes clear that {0} is no joke. The crowd gasps and cheers as blows are blocked, dodged and traded, and with every successful hit the idea that the champion might finally fall grows within the spectators, yourself included."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.JustWatchFight.PoorThing": "[pg]The poor thing that enters the ring gets viciously knocked out in seconds. The disappointment in Demonfist's face is noticeable, but he shrugs it off and congratulates the loser for {0} effort nonetheless. You can't help but think that sportsmanship doesn't really make up for the bruises and the gem deficit."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.LeaveTent.NodsExit": "[pg]You nod at him and move to the tent's exit, a process that requires quite a bit of pushing and shoving through the densely packed crowd."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.LeaveTent.NotFighting": "You don't really feel like fighting in the ring right now. You tell Ozzie you're leaving, and he shrugs. [say: Alright, suit yourself. More money for me.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.LustKO.CoylyAsks": "[pg]You coyly ask whatever he means by that, jerking your sweating body forward and visibly stunning him in the process."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.LustKO.GrabsJaw": "[pg][say: That's your strategy then, huh?] He grabs his jaw and winces, attempting to get up. [say: Got me, got me. That's a knockout, I'm done.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.LustKO.LethiceTits": "[pg][say: Lethice's tits, can you please take this fight seriously?]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.LustKO.MovementsSlow": "The demon's energetic movements slow down, and you notice he begins to lose focus on the fight."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.LustKO.SpotsOpening": "[pg]Spotting an opening in his defenses, you swiftly uppercut him, hitting him straight on his jaw and causing an explosion of sweat to burst from him, his head whiplashing back in a visibly painful impact. He drops to the ground like a ragdoll, and remains silent for a few moments before groaning in pain."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.LustKO.StopsRambling": "[pg]He stops moving, frustrated, and begins rambling. [say: Damn it, you know what I'm talking about! All this teasing, rubbing, moaning and whatever! Stop that shit right n--]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.MiffixFight.ComingDown": "[pg]Coming down from from his leap, the imp twists his body and attempts to elbow his opponent in the ribs, a move that, to the audience's sheer amazement, lands successfully, causing the demon to twist in pain and bringing his head low, to a level the imp can reach without jumping."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.MiffixFight.DoesNotGetUp": "[pg]The imp does not get up."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.MiffixFight.FightStarts": "[pg]Demonfist smiles. [say: That's it then! The fight starts after you throw the first punch. Come on!] he says, cheekily taunting the imp by waving his hand in a \"come hither\" motion."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.MiffixFight.GathersCourage": "[pg]The imp gathers his courage, cracks his knuckles, breathes deeply, and then suddenly dashes towards the indigo demon, with a speed far greater than you though he could muster. The rest of the crowd gasps in surprise as well, the very fact the imp is fighting at all already exceeding their expectations."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.MiffixFight.GotTheGems": "[pg][say: Now, Miffix, got the gems?] Demonfist asks, jumping and punching the air, keeping himself heated up. The imp nods, untying a hefty pouch of gems from his loincloth. He throws it towards Demonfist, who quickly grabs it and tosses it out of the ring. The rhino-morph from before takes it, perfectly positioned to receive the impressive amount of gems. [say: Good! Very good! We can start whenever you want! Remember, I can handle dirty fighting, bladed weapons, poisoned fangs, or whatever you may have in store, but this is a <b>physical</b> fight! No lame magic in my ring! Understood?]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.MiffixFight.MiffixSwallows": "[pg]Miffix swallows, attempting to calm himself down. [say: Y-yes. I do.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.MiffixFight.MiffixTerrified": "You look at Miffix. He's evidently terrified, but resolute; it's clear he's not going to back down from this fight."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.MiffixFight.QuickJab": "[pg]Miffix attempts a quick jab as soon as Demonfist enters his range, but the champion swiftly dodges to the right. The demon then attempts a counter hook, but, to your surprise, it whiffs, the imp managing to move back and just barely avoid the powerful strike. Sensing an opportunity due to Demonfist being off-balance, Miffix attempts to finish the fight immediately with an uppercut, jumping with the help of his wings to reach the demon's jaw. Demonfist is fast enough to tilt his head back and avoid the attack, but also shifts his field of view away from his opponent."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.MiffixFight.WastesNoTime": "[pg]Miffix wastes no time, executing a punch aimed straight at Demonfist's face to knock him out cold. In the blink of an eye, however, the indigo demon manages to recover, twisting his body around Miffix's stretched arm and sliding behind the overconfident imp. At the end of his move, the demon launches a powerful elbow hit to the back of Miffix's head, launching him forward and knocking him out."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.MiffixFight2.CheersUnconscious": "[pg]The crowd follows through, cheering for the unconscious imp. Demonfist wipes some of his sweat with a nearby towel, and tells the crowd that that's all the fighting for today. They quickly disperse, scattered commentaries about the day's fights filling the air, including some complaints about the obscenely long streak of victories. You follow the rest of the crowd, wondering if you should give Demonfist a shot yourself in the future."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.MiffixFight2.CrowdSilent": "The crowd remains silent for a moment before cheering for their undefeated champion. Demonfist rubs his bruised ribs a couple times before waving at the rhino-morph, who quickly does his job and takes Miffix away."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.MiffixFight2.GoodSmartOne": "[pg][say: Good, smart one! If that punch had a little more power, I might have been stunned for long enough for him to finish me off. Not good enough, but cheers to that brave little bastard!]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.NameYourself.MustNameYourself": "<b>You must name yourself.</b>"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.PlayerWins.ApproachesGrabsWrist": "[pg]Demonfist gets up and approaches you, grabbing your wrist with a tired smile. [say: I own this crappy tent, so I think I've the right to say this now. [ringname] here is the new Champion!] He lifts your arm, and the crowd begins to cheer for you, yelling out your name with fervor and admiration. You can't help but smile and raise your other arm in a victorious fist pump. Today, you are the {0} of Mareth! Or of a certain small corner of the Bazaar. Either way, it feels good."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.PlayerWins.CrowdSilent": "The crowd remains silent, with only the occasional whisper being heard in the tent."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.PlayerWins.IncubusBreaks": "[pg]Finally, an incubus decides to break the silence. [say: [He] cheated! [He] must have used magic, that's the only way [he] could have moved so fast! Not only that, bu--]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.PlayerWins.ShutHellUp": "[pg][say: Shut the hell up, you moron]--Demonfist yells out, instantly silencing the incubus--[say: [Ringname] here beat me fair and square. Maybe I fought too much today already or maybe I got complacent over the hundreds of victories I've had, but the truth is that I've been bested.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.QuestionTheBazaar.EveryNonDemon": "[pg][say: What did you expect? Every last non demon killed or enslaved? Everything south of the mountains burnt to ashes?]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.QuestionTheBazaar.FervorFaded": "[pg]You ask him what happened to her \"fervor\" with time. His expression lightens, looking a bit distant, remembering the past."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.QuestionTheBazaar.GroansConcedes": "[pg]He groans, but concedes. Partially."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.QuestionTheBazaar.HeFrowns": "[pg]He frowns. He was ready for the question, but not necessarily ready to give a proper answer. It comes out with a surprising amount of anger, as if he's been asked that in the past."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.QuestionTheBazaar.HowPossible": "[pg]This coexistence. How is it possible?"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.QuestionTheBazaar.ImpossibleAfterAll": "[pg]Perhaps coexistence is impossible, after all."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.QuestionTheBazaar.ItDawns": "[pg]It dawns on you; He wasn't asked this question before: He has asked that question to himself."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.QuestionTheBazaar.JustVanished": "[pg][say: It just vanished. We brought her gems, slaves, a variety of artifacts and unthinkable amounts of lethicite. Yet, as the days passed, she became apathetic to what she started. And one day, it became clear that she didn't care. She continued to issue orders and to tax our plunder merely to impose her authority. There was no plan for the end of the war, but it came, suddenly. What to do, then?]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.QuestionTheBazaar.LooksAround": "You look around the Black Cock and notice its curious assortment of patrons. Humanoids of varying species, succubi, incubi, terrible bards, one lost person from Ingnam, and one old retired soldier from a demonic army. Even with a quick glance, you notice the unspoken tension between the demons and the other denizens. The barmaids approach them with caution, the other patrons give them a noticeable berth. Still, it's not what you would have expected from the race that ushered in an apocalyptic war so few years ago."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.QuestionTheBazaar.NarrowsEyes": "[pg]You narrow your eyes, trying to comprehend what made the Bazaar possible. The carefree demon sitting in front of you is quick to notice your changing expression, and he lays his mug on the table, preparing for a question. You look at him, and it somehow feels like he knows the type of question you're going to ask him."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.QuestionTheBazaar.NoFuckingWay": "[pg][say: No fucking way, [name]. If the Bazaar grew big enough to be called \"civilization\", then it wouldn't take a week for demons to raze it to the ground. We couldn't resist the temptation. I certainly wouldn't.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.QuestionTheBazaar.NotTired": "[pg][say: We didn't get tired of the raiding, the raping, the feeling of wielding power. But there was nothing left, and, despite everything, we were still living things. We had to live, and you can't rely on demons to restore civilization on their own. The Bazaar was born out of this, I believe.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.QuestionTheBazaar.OrganizesThoughts": "[pg-]You organize your thoughts and ask him if he knows how the Bazaar was created, and, most importantly, how it doesn't fall apart when a great portion of its inhabitants are, quite literally, soulless demons."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.QuestionTheBazaar.QuickToPointOut": "[pg]You're quick to point out that that is, indeed, the fate of many of the towns and villages in Mareth."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.QuestionTheBazaar.RepeatsBelieve": "[pg]You [i: believe]? He sighs as you repeat that word to him. [say: Yeah, I wasn't around when it started. Can't say who was, really. Demons aren't fond of keeping history, and the others, well, they're just trying to survive. No time to care about such details when you're living with the same people that destroyed your world.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.QuestionTheBazaar.Repositioning": "[pg][say: That's how it was in the beginning], he says, repositioning himself on his chair and hunching forward towards you, [say: when Lethice's fervor was at its greatest, and, by extension, ours. We were ready and willing to wield our power to get whatever we could, and Mareth was ripe for the picking. Nothing could stop us, and we weren't going to stop ourselves. She ordered us to take everything we could and raze what we couldn't. We were happy to oblige.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.QuestionTheBazaar.StaresDeep": "[pg]You frown and stare deep into his eyes. He doesn't flinch, merely raising an eyebrow. He means it, absolutely."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.QuestionTheBazaar.ThinksWords": "[pg]You think on his words for a moment. The Bazaar is a fragile shard of civilization, born after the apocalyptic war the demons waged. An example of what a world with a more peaceful coexistence between demons and marethians could have been? You explain your thought to him, and he laughs ruefully."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.RegularPlayerLoss.BreathesDeeply": "[pg]You breathe deeply, groan and stand up."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.RegularPlayerLoss.CheersChange": "[pg]The crowd's cheers swiftly change from a mix of mockery and cheers to full support, Demonfist's words motivating them to motivate you. He might be right. The next move may give you the victory!"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.RegularPlayerLoss.CrowdDisappointed": "[pg]The crowd's reaction is a mix of disappointment and relief, some of the audience expecting a victory, while others glad their bets were successful. Demonfist himself breathes deeply, swiping the sweat off his forehead before extending a hand to help you get up."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.RegularPlayerLoss.DropsGround": "[pg]You then drop to the ground, exhausted."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.RegularPlayerLoss.HellOfShow": "[say: You gave them a hell of a show, and myself a run for my gems. Take care of those bruises, I'll be waiting for a rematch. I got a feeling the next one won't be that easy for me.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.RegularPlayerLoss.PullingYouUp": "[pg-][say: There we go]--He says, while pulling you up--"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.RegularPlayerLoss.ReadiesWeapon": "[pg]You ready your [weapon], focusing your gaze on your opponent."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.RegularPlayerLoss.SlapsBack": "[pg] He slaps you firmly on the back and leads you towards the exit. You nod at him, fatigued, but motivated to improve and try again."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.RegularPlayerLoss.StumblesBack": "You stumble back, panting heavily, [legs] on the verge of buckling. Demonfist urges you on, motioning you to charge after him. [say: Come on, [Ringname], there's gotta be more fight left in you! Come on, the next attack may be all it takes for you to win!]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.RegularPlayerLoss.TrainAndReturn": "[say: You're getting there, [Ringname]. Train a bit and ready yourself. I can tell this isn't your best, and that's what I want to see.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.RegularPlayerLoss.TrainMore": "[say: You should train a bit more before stepping into the ring, [Ringname]. You have potential, but you're not going to see it flourish if you're too eager to prove yourself. I'm not going anywhere.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.RhinoExplanation.CutsYouOff": "[pg]You open your mouth to answer, but he cuts you off. [say: Good. Come in, I think we have a good prospect already.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.RhinoExplanation.DemonfistLeaves": "[say: Demonfist told me he has to leave the Bazaar for now. To train, lift boulders, suplex frost giants, you know how these types are. He realized he's been slacking off, and you were his wake up call. Anyway, doesn't matter for now. I run this joint until he comes back, and I'm changing the rules a bit.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.RhinoExplanation.FinishesSentence": "[pg]Just as he finishes his sentence, the black dog-morph delivers a powerful kick to the demon's ribs, stunning him. The crowd cheers as he readies his daggers and lunges towards the demon; He stops at the very last moment and, instead of stabbing or slicing him, merely strikes a light jab on the demon's chin, knocking him out. [say: Heh, nice, isn't it?] The rhino-morph says, staring amusedly at you. [say: Well, if you want to fight him, just tell me. My name's Ozzie, by the way, and the mutt's <DOG_NAME>.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.RhinoExplanation.OpensFlap": "[pg]He pulls open the tent's entrance flap and motions you in. The uncomfortable heat and the smell of blood and sweat hits you again, still just as uncomfortable as the last time, but you go inside anyway. Your eyes are immediately attracted to the ring, where a grizzled looking dog-morph seems to be toying with his opponent, a heavily muscled, menacing looking, and hopelessly exhausted crimson demon. [say: You're the champion now, but you're not going to fight every piss-drinking imp that has enough gems in his pocket. It's a free for all, and the best fighter of the day gets a fight with you. You can defend your title as many times as you want, as long as you're willing to pay. Good enough for you?]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.RhinoExplanation.OpensPath": "[pg]The rhino morph opens a path through the spectators inside to lead you right next to the ring. He points to a bloodied and weathered stool--the one Demonfist used to sit on--and motions for you to get comfortable.[if (!isBiped) { He quickly realizes you're not really capable of sitting like that, but shrugs it off, gesturing to just do whatever works for you.}]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.RhinoExplanation.TalksSpectators": "[pg]He talks to a few of the spectators, taking a few gems and laughing a bit before heading towards you again, still looking at the fight. [say: I figure that's going to be your opponent. The mangy mutt there--bastard's been wiping the floor with everyone here. Seems Demonfist's defeat gave him the motivation he needed to try his luck. I believe you'll need some of it yourself.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.RhinoExplanation.WillConsider": "You tell him you'll consider it, and he nods before entering the ring to declare the winner and pull the fatigued loser out. The grizzled dog-morph sheathes his daggers, breathes deeply and calmly steps out of the ring, merging with the crowd."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.TentDescriptionDemonfistIn.AnotherRound": "It's your chance to get another round in the ring."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.TentDescriptionDemonfistIn.BackToArena": "You make your way back to Demonfist's arena. The line is as packed and the crowd as energetic today as the first time you watched him. This time around Miffix is nowhere to be seen, making the wait a fair bit more tedious. You can endure it for a shot at the champion, however."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.TentDescriptionDemonfistIn.ChampionRitual": "[pg]The champion does his usual short rest ritual before getting up from his stool again and pointing at the audience, calling for another fighter insane enough to take him on. "
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.TentDescriptionDemonfistIn.FinallyInside": "[pg]After several minutes, you finally make your way inside the tent, the heat and smell still rather uncomfortable. You position yourself as close to the ring as you can, eager to shout your name whenever Demonfist finishes off his current opponent. It isn't long before it happens, a well placed and viciously fast uppercut knocking out {0} cold to the audience's amazement."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.TentDescriptionDemonfistIn.LacksGems": "Unfortunately, you lack the gems to get a shot at the champion. Perhaps it's for the best, you think to yourself."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.TentDescriptionDemonfistIn.YourChance": "It's your chance! You could scream your name and get in the ring, though perhaps it isn't be a good idea to do so."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.TentDescriptionDemonfistOut.BackToArena": "You make your way back to Demonfist's arena. The line is as packed as ever, but this time you hear murmurs and gossip from spectators and would-be challengers alike. [say: Demonfist is gone!] a rotund looking demon exclaims loudly. [say: Got his ass beat by that [ringname] fellow, now he doesn't have the courage to show his face around here!] He crosses his arms, sure his theory is correct."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.TentDescriptionDemonfistOut.BackToArenaAgain": "You make your way back to Demonfist's arena. The line is still intimidating, but the people in it allow you to cut in and enter the tent quickly and with minimal resistance, owing to your privileged status. The stuffy air and sounds of fighting and cheering are oddly invigorating to you now; You feel your limbs itching for a fight."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.TentDescriptionDemonfistOut.DeepVoice": "[pg]Suddenly, you hear an incredibly deep, booming voice. [say: Calm the fuck down, or I'll make sure no one here will be able to [i: stand] in a line ever again!] The crowd calms down for a moment and you turn your head to the source of the voice. At the entrance to the tent proper, you see the rhino-morph that handles Demonfist's money. [say: Good. Keep the fighting inside the ring, you moro-]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.TentDescriptionDemonfistOut.LiftsHead": "[pg]He narrows his eyes and lightly lifts his head, looking in your direction. A moment later, his eyes widen and he marches towards you, easily splitting the crowd open as if they were bushes in a jungle. [say: Hey, you! What the fuck are you doing in line? C'mere!]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.TentDescriptionDemonfistOut.NodsEntrance": "[pg]He approaches you and nods towards the entrance to the tent, a clear path now opened for you. The two of you walk calmly towards it, no one daring to challenge the mountain of muscle or the one that beat Demonfist. He scratches his chin before speaking, the skin on it so thick that it sounds like rocks scraping against each other. [say: Well, [ringname], here's the thing.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.TentDescriptionDemonfistOut.ShutYourMouth": "[pg][say: You shut your fat mouth,] a disheveled looking cat-morph says, clawed finger pointing at the demon, [say: He's coming back! He's just late! Spent too much time training!]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.TentDescriptionDemonfistOut.SlapsAway": "[pg]The demon snorts and mockingly slaps away the cat-morph's finger. This quickly turns to pushing, and before long the line becomes a mess of screaming, shoving and worse. You're caught in the middle of it, and it becomes clear that you'll have to resort to violence to get away unscathed."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.WhatNext.AsksIntentions": "You ask him what he intends to do now that he isn't the champion of his own fighting arena."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.WhatNext.HeShrugs": "[pg]He shrugs. [say: That fat rhino man's got the management of the join covered. I've talked about doing something like this to him before. He'll probably make it a free for all, and, in my absence, I bet there'll be a few decent fighters showing up that were too shy to challenge ol' Demonfist themselves. Now that you beat me, though? Anything's possible.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.WhatNext.MakesSense": "[pg]You think to yourself. Makes sense that people would want to claim your throne now that they're reminded that victory is a possibility at all."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.WhatNext.NoncommittalNod": "[pg]You make a noncommittal nod and ask him what will happen to the tent if he's \"going out there\" to practice."
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.WhatNext.SlamsMug": "[pg]He slams his mug of ale on the table with enough strength to surprise you that it didn't shatter into a dozen pieces. [say: Truth is, beating so many challengers so easily weakened me. Why bother improving, when mediocrity is enough? A good fighter needs to challenge himself. Needs to kiss the ring, taste his own split lips, feel his own bruises and broken bones. That's how you improve. So what do I intend to do now? Well...]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.WhatNext.SmilesAgain": "[pg]Demonfist smiles again, trying to read your expression. [say: And I'm hoping you're committed to showing these usurpers how bitter the ring's floor can be. Hopefully you learn a few tricks your self before I come back and kick your ass.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.WhatNext.StopsSwig": "[pg]He stops a swig of his mug midway through with a stern face. To your surprise, it turns into an enthusiastic smile soon afterwards. [say: Do you really think losing demotivates any fighter worth his salt? No. Exactly the opposite. I've been waiting for someone like you for a long time.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.WhatNext.SwipesFinger": "[pg]He swipes a finger on a small drop of ale that escaped from his mug and landed on the table and licks it. With a short chuckle, he narrows his eyes. [say: Gonna go out there and see how much I forgot and how much I can learn about fighting. Then I'm gonna give you another shot. If you're willing, of course. But I doubt you won't.]"
  "Scenes.Demonfistfighterscene.WhatNext.VoicePalpable": "[pg]The enthusiasm in his voice is palpable. Seems he's really getting a little motivated."
}
